# {{DISPLAY_NAME_MD}}

This is a LibHandheld source contribution, not an installable device plugin. Its identity comes
from sanitized Device Lab evidence. No hardware transport or supported-device registration is
generated. `contribution.json` records observed facts, not implemented capabilities.

- Manufacturer: `{{MANUFACTURER_MD}}`
- Baseboard: `{{BOARD_MD}}`
- SKU: `{{SYSTEM_SKU_MD}}`
- BIOS: `{{BIOS_MD}}`
- USB: `{{USB_MD}}`

Copy C# files into `src/LibHandheld/Families/<family>` in the LibHandheld checkout. The identity
uses public `LibHandheld.Contracts` types; no WSGM assembly is referenced. A report also produces
`DeviceProfile.cs`, retaining confirmed buttons, axis maps, observed roles and report provenance
as research data. Unconfirmed fields remain unconfirmed.

Implement the native engine using `Families/MsiClaw` or `Families/RogAlly` and the internal engine
contract as examples. Register only a completed engine in `HandheldDevice`, with exact identity
and capabilities. HC is the Windows authority; cross-check HHD and cite source revisions and
local evidence. Never infer firmware writes from button observations.

`ReportDecoder.cs` rejects every report until fixture-backed decoding is added. Capture starters
include recorded `fixtures/` with exact-source SHA-256 metadata. For separate exports use
`wsgm-device fixture --from <capture> --out-dir <new-directory>`. Add short,
unknown-ID and valid-report cases under `tests/LibHandheld.Tests`. Keep private captures out of
the PR; include sanitized evidence and provenance.

Build and review in the LibHandheld solution. Hardware acceptance remains attended. Submit source,
fixtures and evidence as a LibHandheld PR; do not pack or install a DLL. Complete the contributor
placeholder in the included MIT license before submission.
